tpmute turns the ThinkPad embedded controller's speaker mute into a devd
event, so that user programs can wait for it instead of polling
dev.acpi_ibm.0.mute:

    !system=ACPI subsystem=IBM type=MUTE state=0|1

A kernel thread polls the mute (hw.tpmute.interval_ms) and calls
devctl_notify() on a change. On the ThinkPad A475 it also sets the speaker
mute LED from the EC's mute (hw.tpmute.led).
